From 43bb4394cfba8a9373295b4e01ce1c782d169209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodrigo de Oliveira Ramos
 <89891427+Rodrigo-O-Ramos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:38:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] d4r-check: report the GPU and kernel set the bridge uses

The install check took the first KFD GPU node and looked only for
kernels/<target>. The bridge picks the GPU with the most SIMDs (an
integrated GPU is often listed first, e.g. on Ryzen 7000), honours
D4R_GPU_ARCH, and serves <target>-fp8 on RDNA4 with NativeFp8 and the
marked accuracy/<target> set with PreferAccuracy. On such systems the
check reported the iGPU and said its kernels were missing, and it never
noticed a missing accuracy set.

Mirror the bridge: most SIMDs, D4R_GPU_ARCH, and the selection in
tools/d4r_native_selection.h for the release layout, reading NativeFp8,
PreferAccuracy and NativeKernels from d4r.ini (any key case, inline
comments, CRLF) with the environment winning. The tests compare the
reported folder with the C selection for every target and setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fnL42WqrmG5ACLLvtKRXu
